      "name": "php2shell one week later: Why one exploit doesn\u2019t work everywhere",
      "description": "Several websites went offline as a precaution, as described in our threat actor response blog post . With Log4Shell (CVE-2021-44228), attackers only had to send a short piece of text to a vulnerable application, for example in a login form or a web request. On October 26, CISA added CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog.",
